# Monorepo root .env — HOST-PORT overrides only, for the root dev stack (`make up`, `make seed`,
# which pass it as --env-file). Copy to .env and uncomment what you need, e.g. to run the dev
# stack next to a standalone stack or a second worktree without port clashes.
#
# Standalone stacks (`make -C services/<svc> up`) don't read this file; override their ports
# in the shell instead:  BACKEND_OT_HTTP_PORT=18000 make -C services/backend-ot up
#
# Service configuration does NOT belong here: each service reads its own
# services/<svc>/.env (see that service's .env.example).
#
# Port registry (defaults) — keep in sync with the root CLAUDE.md:
#   backend-ot     http 8000 · postgres 5435 · redis 6380
#   mock-modbus    modbus 502
#   optimizer      8010 (reserved)
#   powerflow      8020 (reserved)
#   frontend       5173 (reserved)

# BACKEND_OT_HTTP_PORT=8000
# BACKEND_OT_POSTGRES_PORT=5435
# BACKEND_OT_REDIS_PORT=6380
# MOCK_MODBUS_PORT=502

# (Standalone backend-ot's aggregator target is also a shell override, not a root .env key:
#  BACKEND_OT_AGGREGATOR_HOST / BACKEND_OT_AGGREGATOR_PORT, default host.docker.internal:502.
#  The dev stack always reads the mock-modbus service.)
